[[Waribá]] grew to approximately 200,000 as the hospitality hub. [[Tabakurí]] reached approximately 90,000 as the capital and government centre. [[Barikú]] reached approximately 55,000. [[Waku Bá]] grew to approximately 35,000 as the new northwestern city continued to expand.

